        "Monte le combo"
      ]
    },
    "en": {
      "tagline": "A marble machine to keep running. Unlock the gates before they overflow and move the socket to catch the electric marble.",
      "tags": [
        "Tap to unlock",
        "Catch the spark",
        "Build the combo"
      ]
    }
  },
  "description": "A marble machine in portrait, and the player keeps it running. A feed gear turning half off the screen pours marbles onto chrome rails with real slope physics: they pick up speed downhill, slow on the flat and crawl over the top of a loop, through flip-flop switches, a notched wheel that merges lines, zigzags, corkscrews, coils, whirlpools that drain through their centre, glass tubes, pipes that dive behind the machine and resurface and ferry gears that carry a marble round their rim from one line to the next, into glowing arrivals at the bottom, each known by its colour. What they swallow drops to a gutter and rides a screw tower up the back of the machine to the feed gear, so the pour never runs dry. Every marble delivered climbs the combo on the wheel hub, and the combo multiplies every point. The gates are open until one LOCKS, at random and more and more often: a locked gate holds its marbles in slots that fill green to red and shows a big pulsing padlock, and a tap opens it. A marble that reaches a full locked gate breaks the combo and drops through a trapdoor behind the machine, where a spill network of back rails and turning cogs carries it to a red socket that costs a heart. One ELECTRIC marble is always in play, and one arrival is its socket: the switches flip on their own at every marble that passes, so the player reads the route and taps an arrival to move the socket under it. Caught, the electric marble pays big, sends an arc up the rails to the hub and makes the combo jump — anywhere else it fizzles, the combo breaks and the machine's lights go out for half a second. The machine grows with the climb: five biomes, five machines, each its own skeleton, from one switch and two arrivals to six switches, six gates and six arrivals.",
